{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Morning. I'll get your blood pressure before Doctor Naidoo calls you. Arm out, please.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Ag, this is a waste of time. I'm not properly sick.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): Blood pressure is one forty eight over ninety two. Pulse is seventy eight. Oxygen sat is ninety seven percent.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): That's basically normal for me. The parking was hectic, hey. Can we just get on with it?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (DOCTOR): Sorry, sorry, this thing has frozen on the prescription screen. Right. What's the problem today?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): It's nothing. Um, a little cough. Just a cold, that's all.",
  "[SEG0007] person_4 (CAREGIVER): Doctor, he's been coughing for weeks. Dry cough. It wakes him at night.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (DOCTOR): Hang on, say that again? I was clicking the wrong tab.",
  "[SEG0009] person_4 (CAREGIVER): Dry cough, about three weeks, maybe a bit more. No phlegm that I've seen.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Shame, she's making a fuss. It hung on after a cold. I'm fine.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (DOCTOR): When did that cold start? Repeat it, the dates on here are a mess.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know. Beginning of the month-ish. It wasn't even a bad one.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any fever with this? Chest pain? Shortness of breath?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No fever, no chest pain. I walk to the shop, no drama.",
  "[SEG0015] person_4 (CAREGIVER): He does get puffed on the stairs at night when the cough is going. He just won't say so.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Ag no. That's me being unfit, not breathless. Don't write that down.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'm in your medication list now. You were started on ramipril recently, is that right?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja, the new blood pressure tablet. Um, ramipril, well, actually, ja, ramipril, five milligrams, every morning. About three weeks back, from the chemist.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (DOCTOR): Five milligrams? Say the dose again, the screen jumped.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Five milligrams. Once in the morning. I swallow it, by mouth. Obviously.",
  "[SEG0021] person_4 (CAREGIVER): His brother takes lisinopril, twenty milligrams, and he coughs nonstop. That's the brother's tablet, not his.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (DOCTOR): Okay. The brother's lisinopril is not his. I'm not putting that on his script.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): I've had the high blood pressure for five-ish years. Before the ramipril they had me on the water tablet.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (DOCTOR): Which water tablet? I need you to repeat the name, I've lost the line.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Hydrochlorothiazide. Twelve point five milligrams. They stopped it because the pressure was still up. I don't take it anymore.",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (NURSE): Just so it's on the note, doctor, pressure one forty eight over ninety two, pulse seventy eight, sats ninety seven percent. I did those outside.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (DOCTOR): Thanks, sister. Let me have a listen, deep breath for me. Lungs are clear, no wheeze. Throat's not red either.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): See? Nothing there. I told you it's a cold.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'm thinking out loud, so don't jump on it. A dry cough a few weeks after starting ramipril can be the ACE inhibitor. It can also just be the tail of that cold. I'm not calling it a ramipril cough, and I'm not ruling the cold out.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): So you agree with me. It's the cold.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): I didn't agree. Both are still possible. What I am doing is stopping the ramipril from today and changing you to losartan.",
  "[SEG0032] person_4 (CAREGIVER): Does he finish the ramipril he's got at home?",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (DOCTOR): No. Stop it. Losartan fifty milligrams, by mouth, once every morning, starting tomorrow, for the blood pressure.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Fifty against five. Sounds hectic, but ja, I'll take it if you say so.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (DOCTOR): Different drug, different strength. Any allergies?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No allergies. Never have.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (DOCTOR): If the cough is still there in three weeks, we'll arrange a chest X-ray. I'm not booking it now.",
  "[SEG0038] person_4 (CAREGIVER): And when must he come back for the pressure?",
  "[SEG0039] person_3 (DOCTOR): Come back in four weeks either way, so I can recheck it. If your face swells or you can't breathe, don't wait for that, go to casualty.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja, ja. It'll be gone. You're all worrying for nothing.",
  "[SEG0041] person_3 (DOCTOR): Bring the losartan box to that visit so we're sure of the tablet. Reception will book the four weeks.",
  "[SEG0042] person_1 (NURSE): Come, I'll take you to the front desk."
 ],
